 // V18.14: Replace Article 50 text only.
 if(viewArticles[49]) viewArticles[49].text="Today, seeing the love, patience and dedication shown to children living with disabilities made me stop for a moment and reflect.\n\nNot just on those children, but on the countless people who quietly dedicate so much of their lives to making life a little easier for others.\n\nCarers, nurses, therapists, teachers, volunteers, parents, families and so many others whose kindness and dedication we sometimes take for granted.\n\nOver the years, life has given me quite a few opportunities to experience both sides of human nature. I've seen kindness where I least expected it and I've experienced what it feels like to be completely helpless, dependent on others for even the simplest things in life.\n\nThere is an enormous difference between being looked after and feeling cared for.\nA nurse who takes an extra moment to listen. Someone who patiently helps you do something you've been struggling with. A reassuring smile when you're frightened. A little humour when everything seems rather hopeless or simply someone who treats you as a human being rather than another patient, another wheelchair, another problem to solve.\n\nSometimes it's the smallest gestures that leave the deepest impressions.\n\nSo to all those \"Angels\" out there who spends their days helping children, elderly people, people living with disabilities, illness or simply those who can no longer manage everything on their own...\n\n𝗧𝗵𝗮𝗻𝗸 𝗬𝗼𝘂 ❤️";
